## Frequently Asked Questions

### Q: Can Samsung Find locate a phone that is turned off?
A: Not live. Samsung says that when a phone is powered off, only its last known location is available, and only if **Send last location** was on. Offline finding works when the phone is on but has no connection.

### Q: Is Samsung Find the same as Find My Mobile?
A: Samsung Find is the current app and website for locating a Galaxy. Find My Mobile is a name you'll still see in the phone's settings, under Lost device protection. To locate a lost phone, use Samsung Find.

### Q: Can I find my Samsung phone without a Samsung account?
A: Not with Samsung Find. Try Google's Find Hub at [google.com/android/find](https://www.google.com/android/find), which uses the Google account on the phone.

### Q: Should I use Samsung Find or Google's Find Hub?
A: Both. They're separate services with separate accounts, and a Galaxy phone can have both switched on. If one can't locate the phone, try the other.

### Q: How do I lock my Samsung phone if it's stolen?
A: Sign in at samsungfind.samsung.com, select the phone and choose **Lock**. You set a PIN and can add a contact number and a message for the lock screen.

### Q: Does Samsung Find take a photo of the thief?
A: No. Samsung Find shows the phone's location and lets you ring, lock or erase it. To get a photo of someone who tries to unlock the phone, you need an app like CrookCatcher, installed beforehand.

